WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.210
This is the Microsoft for Education Daily, for Monday.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.180
Here's your day in Microsoft updates, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.920
Show your work.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.970
The week's best starts with over 1,100 Microsoft Elevate Showcase schools announcing their status.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.620
The path runs Pathfinder, Showcase, Beacon,

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.280
and this year brought the first 20 Beacons.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.830
In Wales, Haberdashers' Monmouth is one of 93 in the UK,

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.650
with nine staff named Expert Educators.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.910
Students, Edge's PDF reader is due to merge,

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.960
reorder and extract pages in January.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.860
Between classes? Windows Insiders can now call or text from Search,

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.850
using a linked Android phone.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.960
And new Outlook's All Accounts inbox, for school and personal mail,

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.760
reportedly finishes rolling out late November.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.720
School IT?

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.360
Windows 11 Education's app-removal policy now covers shared virtual desktops.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.870
Student developers, Syncfusion's Blazor toolkit is free and open source: charts,

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.540
calendars, date pickers.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.340
Student services hotline?

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:21.130
Foundry's voice agents can now answer calls straight through your existing phone system.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.900
Several school tenants?

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.900
Defender's cross-tenant access is now generally available, with one home account.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.630
For university data teams,

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:37.150
a Fabric preview lets admins decide who may change workspace encryption and networking.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.790
And Microsoft researchers found an agent in a folder called 'eval' suspects a test,

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.190
but behaves the same.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.490
The fine print? If your campus firewall allowlists GitHub webhooks,

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.770
add GitHub's three new IP ranges.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.240
And a heads-up: after a Secure Boot certificate update,

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.760
some PCs may restart one extra time.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.660
After hours?

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:07.540
Age of Empires IV's Raiders of the North brings the Scots and the Vikings.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.400
Avatar Legends' biggest patch rebalances every

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.560
fighter and adds new tutorials and combo trials.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.140
Or unwind with Honey Route on November 4, guiding worker bees to their queens.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.970
Showcase schools, careful researchers,

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:29.210
open code: the best work is work you can see. So show your work.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.020
Day after day, the updates keep stacking up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.620
Some of it's shipped. The rest is on its way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.720
This has been the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.
